  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Verizon Business Network Services recorded $407M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Verizon Business Network Services won 376 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.1M and obligations down 6.6% year over year. Verizon Business Network Services has seen obligations vary across recent years: FY21 $265M, FY22 $496M, FY23 $380M, FY24 $459M, FY25 $436M, FY26 $407M. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer this year at $115M, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services at $101M and the Department of Justice at $61.1M. Wired Telecommunications Carriers dominate Verizon Business Network Services’ markets at $353M, with Wireless Telecommunications Carriers (except Satellite) at $28.8M and Telecommunications Resellers at $10.1M. The numbers reported are contract obligations except where noted otherwise for award values in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables. Current-year totals are partial and cover fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has Verizon Business Network Services’ federal business trended recently?",
        "body": "Verizon Business Network Services obligations were $407M in FY2026 to date, down 6.6% year over year. Verizon Business Network Services obligations rose from $265M in FY21 to $496M in FY22, then moved to $380M in FY23, $459M in FY24, and $436M in FY25 before the current-year total of $407M. Verizon Business Network Services reported 376 awards this fiscal year with an average award size of $1.1M. These figures are fiscal year to date and represent obligations, not final annual totals."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the largest buyers and what markets does Verizon Business Network Services serve?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense bought $115M, the Department of Health and Human Services bought $101M, and the Department of Justice bought $61.1M in FY2026 to date. Other top buyers include the Social Security Administration at $29.6M, the Department of the Treasury at $27.4M, and the Department of Commerce at $16.1M. Wired Telecommunications Carriers is the largest market at $353M, followed by Wireless Telecommunications Carriers (except Satellite) at $28.8M and Telecommunications Resellers at $10.1M. Verizon Business Network Services also shows smaller obligations in Other Computer Related Services, Telephone Apparatus Manufacturing, and Facilities Support Services."
      }
    ]
  },
